WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.329 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
The document is open. At

00:00:02.329 --> 00:00:04.658 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the top it says, Q3

00:00:04.658 --> 00:00:05.590 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Innovation Plan.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.453 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
The cursor blinks. Your

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:09.783 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
inbox is full of requests,

00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:12.112 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
your team wants a direction,

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:12.578 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
and

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.441 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
somebody wants a polished

00:00:14.441 --> 00:00:16.770 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
plan by Friday. I know

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:17.702 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
that room.

00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:20.031 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
The pressure makes the blank

00:00:20.031 --> 00:00:22.360 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
page feel like the problem.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.689 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
So you open a tool,

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:27.019 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
ask for ideas, and in

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:29.348 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
thirty seconds you have a

00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:31.520 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
confident looking answer.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.126 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Now what? Who will decide

00:00:34.126 --> 00:00:35.570 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
which idea matters?

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.495 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
What evidence would make

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:38.938 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
that choice responsible?

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.345 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
What data did you put

00:00:41.345 --> 00:00:42.788 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
into the tool

00:00:42.788 --> 00:00:45.195 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
to get there? A beautiful

00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:47.119 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
page can hide those

00:00:47.119 --> 00:00:49.044 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
questions for a little

00:00:49.044 --> 00:00:49.526 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
while.

00:00:49.526 --> 00:00:51.932 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
It cannot answer them. In

00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:53.857 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the opening of Accelerated,

00:00:53.857 --> 00:00:56.263 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
I start with that blinking

00:00:56.263 --> 00:00:56.744 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
cursor

00:00:56.744 --> 00:00:59.150 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
because it is familiar. The

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.075 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
book begins with product

00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:02.519 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
teams carrying noise,

00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:03.963 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
conflicting priorities, and

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:06.369 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
documents that do not move

00:01:06.369 --> 00:01:08.775 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
decisions. The work here is

00:01:08.775 --> 00:01:11.181 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
to give the team a

00:01:11.181 --> 00:01:13.587 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
way to learn, choose, and

00:01:13.587 --> 00:01:15.993 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
keep its judgment when the

00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:17.437 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
page fills up.

00:01:17.437 --> 00:01:19.362 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
A product system sounds

00:01:19.362 --> 00:01:21.768 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
larger than it needs to

00:01:21.768 --> 00:01:22.249 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
be.

00:01:22.249 --> 00:01:24.656 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Think about the last idea

00:01:24.656 --> 00:01:27.062 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
that arrived in a meeting.

00:01:27.062 --> 00:01:28.987 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Someone noticed a customer

00:01:28.987 --> 00:01:31.393 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
problem. Someone else had a

00:01:31.393 --> 00:01:32.355 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
competing story.

00:01:32.355 --> 00:01:34.761 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
A third person asked for

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.168 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
a number nobody had. The

00:01:37.168 --> 00:01:39.093 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
team left with another

00:01:39.093 --> 00:01:39.574 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
document

00:01:39.574 --> 00:01:41.980 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
to write. A system gives

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.386 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
those moments a path. It

00:01:44.386 --> 00:01:46.792 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
helps you record the signal,

00:01:46.792 --> 00:01:48.717 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
name the decision, state

00:01:48.717 --> 00:01:51.123 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
what you believe, and come

00:01:51.123 --> 00:01:53.048 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
back to what happened.

00:01:53.048 --> 00:01:55.454 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
AI can help organize messy

00:01:55.454 --> 00:01:57.861 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
input, test the shape of

00:01:57.861 --> 00:02:00.267 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
an argument, and make a

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.192 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
first draft. The judgment

00:02:02.192 --> 00:02:04.598 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
still belongs to people who

00:02:04.598 --> 00:02:06.042 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
understand the consequences.

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.448 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
That is the argument in

00:02:08.448 --> 00:02:10.373 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the first chapter. I

00:02:10.373 --> 00:02:12.779 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
describe AI as a strategy

00:02:12.779 --> 00:02:13.260 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
partner,

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.666 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
a signal amplifier, and a

00:02:15.666 --> 00:02:17.591 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
structure builder. Those are

00:02:17.591 --> 00:02:19.997 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
jobs it may help with,

00:02:19.997 --> 00:02:20.478 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
under

00:02:20.478 --> 00:02:22.403 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the right conditions. They

00:02:22.403 --> 00:02:24.810 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
are not permission to trust

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.772 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
every output.

00:02:25.772 --> 00:02:28.178 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
If it gives you five

00:02:28.178 --> 00:02:30.103 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
polished options, you still

00:02:30.103 --> 00:02:32.509 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
need to ask who benefits,

00:02:32.509 --> 00:02:32.991 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
what

00:02:32.991 --> 00:02:35.397 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
is missing, and which option

00:02:35.397 --> 00:02:37.803 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
you can test safely. Speed

00:02:37.803 --> 00:02:40.209 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
can create room to think.

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:42.615 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
It can also fill that

00:02:42.615 --> 00:02:44.540 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
room with more noise.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.946 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Look at this map. Signals.

00:02:46.946 --> 00:02:49.352 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Alignment. Momentum. It is a

00:02:49.352 --> 00:02:51.277 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
way to navigate the

00:02:51.277 --> 00:02:51.759 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
workshop.

00:02:51.759 --> 00:02:54.165 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
First, take the raw material

00:02:54.165 --> 00:02:56.571 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
coming at you and find

00:02:56.571 --> 00:02:58.496 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
a question worth answering.

00:02:58.496 --> 00:03:00.421 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Then give the people

00:03:00.421 --> 00:03:02.346 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
carrying the decision a

00:03:02.346 --> 00:03:03.308 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
shared direction.

00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:05.714 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Then build a rhythm that

00:03:05.714 --> 00:03:08.120 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
lets the next round of

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.045 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
evidence change the plan.

00:03:10.045 --> 00:03:11.970 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
The book organizes its

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.895 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
printed chapters as Systems,

00:03:13.895 --> 00:03:15.339 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Align, and Momentum.

00:03:15.339 --> 00:03:17.745 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
The workshop uses the three

00:03:17.745 --> 00:03:19.670 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
labels on this existing

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.595 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
infographic as a visual

00:03:21.595 --> 00:03:22.076 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
guide.

00:03:22.076 --> 00:03:24.482 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
You will see where those

00:03:24.482 --> 00:03:26.889 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
paths cross; the graphic is

00:03:26.889 --> 00:03:29.295 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
not a replacement for the

00:03:29.295 --> 00:03:31.220 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
chapters. In these first

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:33.626 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
lessons we stay close to

00:03:33.626 --> 00:03:35.069 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the signal side.

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:37.476 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
We will choose one decision,

00:03:37.476 --> 00:03:39.401 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
work backward to evidence,

00:03:39.401 --> 00:03:41.807 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
and ask what a small

00:03:41.807 --> 00:03:42.288 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
test

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.694 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
could teach us. There is

00:03:44.694 --> 00:03:47.100 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
a human thread through the

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.506 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
book, too: Sam, a product

00:03:49.506 --> 00:03:51.913 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
manager who has talent but

00:03:51.913 --> 00:03:53.838 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
keeps getting pulled into

00:03:53.838 --> 00:03:54.800 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
reactive work.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.180 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
manager who has talent but

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.125 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
keeps getting pulled into

00:03:57.125 --> 00:03:57.597 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
reactive work.

00:03:57.597 --> 00:03:59.586 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
That story makes the

00:03:59.586 --> 00:04:02.072 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
pressure visible. It is a

00:04:02.072 --> 00:04:04.061 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
teaching story from the

00:04:04.061 --> 00:04:05.055 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
book, not

00:04:05.055 --> 00:04:06.103 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
a claim about a current

00:04:06.103 --> 00:04:06.732 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
customer. Keep that

00:04:06.732 --> 00:04:07.781 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
distinction in view as we

00:04:07.781 --> 00:04:08.200 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
move between

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.786 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
a claim about a current

00:04:10.786 --> 00:04:12.218 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
customer. Keep that

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.604 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
distinction in view as we

00:04:14.604 --> 00:04:15.558 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
move between

00:04:15.558 --> 00:04:17.467 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
story, worksheet, and public

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:17.945 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
proof.

00:04:17.945 --> 00:04:20.331 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Before you try any prompt,

00:04:20.331 --> 00:04:22.240 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
decide what information can

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.671 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
leave your desk.

00:04:23.671 --> 00:04:25.580 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
The book's data-safety note

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.489 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
comes before the chapters

00:04:27.489 --> 00:04:28.921 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
for a reason.

00:04:28.921 --> 00:04:30.352 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Customer details, finances,

00:04:30.352 --> 00:04:31.784 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
internal strategy, and

00:04:31.784 --> 00:04:33.693 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
company records can carry

00:04:33.693 --> 00:04:35.125 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
obligations that a

00:04:35.125 --> 00:04:36.079 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
convenient text

00:04:36.079 --> 00:04:38.465 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
box does not erase. My

00:04:38.465 --> 00:04:40.851 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
working rule for this course

00:04:40.851 --> 00:04:42.760 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
is simple: use public

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.238 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
information,

00:04:43.238 --> 00:04:44.669 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
material your organization

00:04:44.669 --> 00:04:47.055 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
has approved for that use,

00:04:47.055 --> 00:04:48.964 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
or a made-up example.

00:04:48.964 --> 00:04:51.350 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
If you are unsure, stop

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.737 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
and check the policy that

00:04:53.737 --> 00:04:55.168 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
governs your work.

00:04:55.168 --> 00:04:57.077 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Do not put restricted

00:04:57.077 --> 00:04:58.986 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
material into an external

00:04:58.986 --> 00:05:01.372 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
model to make the worksheet

00:05:01.372 --> 00:05:02.327 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
feel realistic.

00:05:02.327 --> 00:05:04.713 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
We can learn the method

00:05:04.713 --> 00:05:06.622 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
with a synthetic case.

00:05:06.622 --> 00:05:09.008 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Imagine a team trying to

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:09.485 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
improve

00:05:09.485 --> 00:05:11.871 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the first week for new

00:05:11.871 --> 00:05:14.257 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
members. We can invent a

00:05:14.257 --> 00:05:16.166 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
harmless request list and

00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:16.644 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
test

00:05:16.644 --> 00:05:18.552 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
our reasoning without using

00:05:18.552 --> 00:05:19.984 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
anyone's account, message,

00:05:19.984 --> 00:05:22.370 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
or history. On the screen,

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.802 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
watch the example

00:05:23.802 --> 00:05:25.711 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
move into a three-column

00:05:25.711 --> 00:05:27.143 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
boundary: public, approved

00:05:27.143 --> 00:05:28.097 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
internal, restricted.

00:05:28.097 --> 00:05:29.529 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
“Approved internal” means

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:30.960 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
approved for this

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.869 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
particular tool and purpose,

00:05:32.869 --> 00:05:35.255 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
not merely available to you

00:05:35.255 --> 00:05:36.210 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
at work.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.119 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
This boundary follows the

00:05:38.119 --> 00:05:40.028 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
decision file through every

00:05:40.028 --> 00:05:42.414 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
lesson. It is part of

00:05:42.414 --> 00:05:43.368 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
product judgment,

00:05:43.368 --> 00:05:44.800 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
not an appendix.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.487 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Let's make the first page

00:05:47.487 --> 00:05:49.974 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
of your decision file. It

00:05:49.974 --> 00:05:52.461 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
starts with a decision, not

00:05:52.461 --> 00:05:54.627 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
a tool. Write one sentence:

00:05:54.627 --> 00:05:56.794 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
“We need to decide whether

00:05:56.794 --> 00:05:58.960 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
to...” It could be whether

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.175 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
to change an onboarding

00:06:01.175 --> 00:06:03.190 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
step, simplify a service

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:05.708 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
request, or test a different

00:06:05.708 --> 00:06:06.715 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
way to

00:06:06.715 --> 00:06:09.234 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
explain an offer. Keep the

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:11.249 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
scope small enough that

00:06:11.249 --> 00:06:13.767 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
someone could make a choice

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:14.271 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
after

00:06:14.271 --> 00:06:16.285 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
seeing evidence. Now write

00:06:16.285 --> 00:06:18.804 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
who owns that choice and

00:06:18.804 --> 00:06:21.322 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
when it must be made.

00:06:21.322 --> 00:06:23.841 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
If nobody owns it, name

00:06:23.841 --> 00:06:26.359 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the role you need to

00:06:26.359 --> 00:06:26.863 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
ask.

00:06:26.863 --> 00:06:28.878 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Underneath, write what would

00:06:28.878 --> 00:06:31.396 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
go wrong if you guessed.

00:06:31.396 --> 00:06:33.915 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Then mark the inputs you

00:06:33.915 --> 00:06:34.418 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
might

00:06:34.418 --> 00:06:36.433 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
want to use. Public,

00:06:36.433 --> 00:06:38.448 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
approved for this purpose,

00:06:38.448 --> 00:06:39.455 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
or restricted.

00:06:39.455 --> 00:06:41.974 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
If the real inputs are

00:06:41.974 --> 00:06:43.988 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
restricted, make a safe

00:06:43.988 --> 00:06:44.492 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
stand-in.

00:06:44.492 --> 00:06:47.010 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Preserve the shape of the

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.025 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
problem; remove the person

00:06:49.025 --> 00:06:51.040 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
and the private facts.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.558 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
You are allowed to pause

00:06:53.558 --> 00:06:56.077 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the video while you write.

00:06:56.077 --> 00:06:58.595 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
When you resume, you should

00:06:58.595 --> 00:07:01.114 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
have a cover sheet a

00:07:01.114 --> 00:07:03.129 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
colleague could read without

00:07:03.129 --> 00:07:03.632 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
asking

00:07:03.632 --> 00:07:06.151 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
what you are trying to

00:07:06.151 --> 00:07:08.669 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
decide. You should also know

00:07:08.669 --> 00:07:11.188 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
which inputs will stay out

00:07:11.188 --> 00:07:13.706 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
of any AI tool. That

00:07:13.706 --> 00:07:16.224 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
is a useful first result,

00:07:16.224 --> 00:07:18.743 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
even if the plan itself

00:07:18.743 --> 00:07:20.254 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
is still unfinished.

00:07:20.254 --> 00:07:22.772 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Take one more look at

00:07:22.772 --> 00:07:25.291 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
your sentence. Could a fast

00:07:25.291 --> 00:07:27.809 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
draft make that decision for

00:07:27.809 --> 00:07:30.328 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
you? Probably not. It might

00:07:30.328 --> 00:07:32.846 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
help you list options, put

00:07:32.846 --> 00:07:34.861 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
questions in order, or

00:07:34.861 --> 00:07:35.365 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
notice

00:07:35.365 --> 00:07:37.883 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
that an assumption is doing

00:07:37.883 --> 00:07:40.402 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
too much work. But a

00:07:40.402 --> 00:07:42.920 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
person still has to decide

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.438 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
what matters and what risk

00:07:45.438 --> 00:07:47.957 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the team is willing to

00:07:47.957 --> 00:07:48.461 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
carry.

00:07:48.461 --> 00:07:50.979 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
That is why I ask

00:07:50.979 --> 00:07:53.497 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
you to keep the decision

00:07:53.497 --> 00:07:54.001 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
file.

00:07:54.001 --> 00:07:56.520 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
A chat window can be

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.038 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
useful for a moment; the

00:07:59.038 --> 00:08:01.053 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
file makes the reasoning

00:08:01.053 --> 00:08:01.557 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
visible

00:08:01.557 --> 00:08:04.075 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
when the moment has passed.

00:08:04.075 --> 00:08:06.593 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Write one line under the

00:08:06.593 --> 00:08:09.112 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
cover: “What would I need

00:08:09.112 --> 00:08:11.630 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
to learn before I choose?”

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.149 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Do not answer it yet.

00:08:14.149 --> 00:08:16.667 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
Let the question sit. In

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:19.186 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the next lesson we will

00:08:19.186 --> 00:08:21.704 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
bring that question into a

00:08:21.704 --> 00:08:23.719 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
crowded planning room. We

00:08:23.719 --> 00:08:26.237 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
will look at three possible

00:08:26.237 --> 00:08:28.756 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
paths and choose one worth

00:08:28.756 --> 00:08:29.259 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
testing.

00:08:29.259 --> 00:08:31.778 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
If you have only a

00:08:31.778 --> 00:08:34.296 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
vague problem now, that is

00:08:34.296 --> 00:08:34.800 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
enough.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:35.947 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
If you have only a

00:08:35.947 --> 00:08:36.894 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
vague problem now, that is

00:08:36.894 --> 00:08:37.083 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
enough.

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:39.687 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
A good first page does

00:08:39.687 --> 00:08:42.291 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
not pretend to know the

00:08:42.291 --> 00:08:42.812 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
answer.

00:08:42.812 --> 00:08:45.035 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
It tells the truth about

00:08:45.035 --> 00:08:46.813 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
the decision, the evidence

00:08:46.813 --> 00:08:48.591 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
you have, and the

00:08:48.591 --> 00:08:49.480 line:78% position:50% size:88% align:middle
information you
